Reads the time zone with musl 1.2.5's code (ports/mlibc/musl/timezone.hpp,
ADR 0194). mlibc's read only a time zone file's version 1 data, which
zic's slim files, its default since 2020, leave empty, and gave every
time after a file's last transition the file's first type, usually
local mean time: in the IANA database's files of today, localtime was
hours off. musl's reads the 64-bit data of version 2 and later files,
the TZ string at their end for the times after their last transition,
and TZ strings with musl's rules. Also:
  - mktime takes a tm_isdst that the zone does not have at that time
    as glibc and musl do, moving the time by the difference;
  - strftime's %Z gives "" for a tm whose zone's name is no longer the
    time zone's, rather than a pointer into a file no longer read;
  - localtime refuses times whose year does not fit an int, with
    EOVERFLOW.
Meant for upstream.

